fig didn't specify it\\n2. The Cisco version automatically enables IPv4 unicast by default (no need for explicit family inet unicast)\\n3. The static route and export policy would need separate translation if needed\", 'trans_template': 'neighbor 172.16.2.2 activate'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'network 172.16.2.0 mask 255.255.255.0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'network 172.16.2.0 mask 255.255.255.0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Cisco IOS commands:\\n\\n##\\nrouter bgp 300\\nneighbor 172.16.2.2 remote-as 300\\nneighbor 172.16.2.2 activate\\nnetwork 172.16.2.0 mask 255.255.255.0\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. I assumed the local AS is 300 (same as peer AS) since the Juniper config didn't specify it\\n2. The Cisco version automatically enables IPv4 unicast by default (no need for explicit family inet unicast)\\n3. The static route and export policy would need separate translation if needed\", 'trans_template': 'network 172.16.2.0 mask 255.255.255.0'}]]": 1,
